<section id="about" class="wrap section" aria-labelledby="about-title" data-section="about">
  <h2 id="about-title">About</h2>
  <div class="col">
    <p>
      I got into this through robots. I competed in FIRST Robotics, and at De Anza I was president of the BattleBots
      club. Now I'm in my third year at San José State, studying computer science and statistics.
    </p>
    <p>
      A robot does what its code tells it. A body is harder to read. The signal from a forearm muscle looks different
      after the sensor comes off and goes back on, and a model trained yesterday starts guessing today. Most of my work
      is catching that change and correcting for it, which is where the statistics turned out to matter.
    </p>
    <p>
      What I want to build is a way of reading those signals that still holds up a month later, so a prosthetic hand
      does what the person wearing it means, every time they put it on.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
